{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1163093-otherworldly-freeholds","id":1163093,"title":"Otherworldly Freeholds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-27T13:19:01-08:00","id":1163093,"title":"Otherworldly Freeholds","content":"A Freehold on Mars - What Do?<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, I had a thought today about what a freehold in a city on Mars might look like. I might just be a tad obsessed with our planetary neighbhor and often dream of going when that becomes a reality. To that end, lately, I've tried to memorize the most likely calendar that we would use, <a href=\"http://ops-alaska.com/time/gangale_converter/calendar_clock.htm\" target=\"_blank\">The Darian Calendar</a>, and my studies in that avenue have led me to look more closely at the seasons of Mars.<br /> <br /> I suppose you can tell where that train of thought ended so here we are:<br /> <br /> Imagine we have colonies on any planet of our solar system (or others). Either artificial housings or legit full/partial terraformed. <br /> <br /> <b>What might a freehold of Lost, within a colony of another planet, look like? </b><br /> <br /> For Mars, I can see the seasonal Courts having little to no power on Mars as the ideas behind them are just not similar. I can see the Northern and Southern hemispheres (or lower and upper regions respectfully) being either very different from each other or the dichotomy of lower and upper being central to the Courts of Mars since there is a significant elevation difference between the North and the South. <br /> <br /> But anyway, I want to hear the musings of others. What about Venus? Titan? IO? Luna?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-28T06:59:22-08:00","id":1163219,"title":"","content":"To start with, I'm going to put aside the origin culture of the colonists - it could very well be something American, but just as likely could be an international coalition, or the Chinese government, or something like we have with Antartica. <br /> <br /> Now, Courts are no longer made by stories. In Rose 2e, we're bound by making a Pact of some kind. You strike a deal. I'm going to assume that, on Mars, you still have daylight cycles, so the day/night courts could transfer over. Other things you can make a deal with on mars: <br /> <br /> * the Elements (frozen icecaps, the red dirt, the atmosphere. <br /> * aspects of the colony, including the agriculture department, the textile department, and the like.<br /> * aspects of the colony buildings - environmental shield-dome, the residential section, etc.<br /> * mix of the three above - the natural Mars, the Place, and the People as three distinct courts.<br /> * specific landmarks<br /> * language based - emoji versus regular language versus computer code.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T06:54:53-08:00","id":1165293,"title":"","content":"Another thought is you could make a pact with the Sun and the moons (Phobos and Deimos). Just off the top of my head... the Sun could represent certainty, life, and such. Deimos could represent the powers of conflict between the forces of Sun and Phobos and the thin line life walks on Mars, while Phobos is uncertainty and terrifying certain fates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}